module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheaf.Basic
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Spec

/-!
# The ideal sheaf extending an ideal of an affine base

Let `f : X ⟶ Spec A` be a morphism of schemes and let `I ⊆ A` be an ideal. The composite
`A ≅ Γ(Spec A, 𝒪) ⟶ Γ(X, 𝒪_X)` carries `I` to an ideal `baseIdeal A I f` of the global
functions on `X`, and the quasi-coherent ideal sheaf it generates is `baseIdealSheaf A I f`.
This is the sheaf written `𝓘 · 𝒪_X` in [Stacks, Section 02O7], and `I ^ n ℱ` there is the
subsheaf of `ℱ` generated by its `n`-th power; the identity
`baseIdealSheaf A (I ^ n) f = baseIdealSheaf A I f ^ n` below is what makes those two readings
of `I ^ n 𝒪_X` agree.

Because `Scheme.IdealSheafData` is presented affine-locally, every statement here reduces to
the corresponding statement about `Ideal.map` of the restriction maps `Γ(X, ⊤) ⟶ Γ(X, U)`, and
`baseIdeal` is a ring-theoretic `Ideal.map`; so `baseIdeal` and `baseIdealSheaf` are
multiplicative, monotone and preserve `⊥` and `⊤`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdeal` — the ideal `I · Γ(X, 𝒪_X)` of global
  functions induced by an ideal of the base ring.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf` — the quasi-coherent ideal sheaf
  `I · 𝒪_X` it generates.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf_pow` — forming the ideal sheaf commutes
  with powers, so the `n`-th power of `I · 𝒪_X` is the ideal sheaf of `I ^ n`.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf_mul` — and with products.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf_mono` — and is monotone.

## Implementation notes

The uniform bound of [Stacks, Tag 02OA] — one integer `c` controlling, in two consecutive
degrees, both the images of `H ^ p(X, I ^ r ℱ) ⟶ H ^ p(X, ℱ)` and the kernels of
`H ^ (p + 1)(X, I ^ k ℱ) ⟶ H ^ (p + 1)(X, ℱ)` — is **not** constructed here, but it is
constructed elsewhere in the library: it is
`Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.exists_uniform_bound_cohomology` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalFunctions/CohomologyIdealPowerSystem.lean`, over the single
named hypothesis `h02O8`.

Its proof rests on that single input, [Stacks, Tag 02O8]: for `A` Noetherian, `f` proper and `ℱ`
coherent, the graded module `⨁ H ^ p(X, I ^ n ℱ)` is finite over the Rees algebra `⨁ I ^ n`.
Nothing weaker suffices: with `c` fixed, the conclusion for `r ⟶ ∞` is exactly the finiteness
statement, so no choice of `c` makes either assertion formal. Tag 02O8 is
`Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.isCohomologyReesFinite_of_sheafSmul`, now standing on the one
sheaf-level identity `Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.ReesSmulCompatible`; the whole chain from
there to [Stacks, Tag 02OC] is assembled in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalFunctions/FormalFunctionsFrom02O8.lean`.

[Stacks, Tag 02O5] — coherence of higher direct images, of which [Stacks, Tag 0897] for the
Rees algebra is a consequence — is proved unconditionally as
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProperCoherenceWitness.higherDirectImageIsCoherent`, and so is its affine case
[Stacks, Tag 02O6].

What is unconditional is the vocabulary: the two definitions below are the ones [Stacks,
Tag 02OA] and the three parts of [Stacks, Tag 02OB] are stated against.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02O7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02O7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02O5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02O5)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I J : Ideal A) {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of A))

/-- The ideal of global functions on `X` generated by the image of an ideal `I` of the base
ring along `f : X ⟶ Spec A`, the composite `A ≅ Γ(Spec A, 𝒪) ⟶ Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`. -/
def baseIdeal : Ideal Γ(X, ⊤) :=
  Ideal.map ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv ≫ f.appTop).hom I

/-- The extension `I · 𝒪_X` to `X` of an ideal `I` on its affine base: the quasi-coherent
ideal sheaf generated by the global functions in `baseIdeal A I f`. -/
def baseIdealSheaf : X.IdealSheafData :=
  .ofIdealTop (baseIdeal A I f)

/-- Affine-locally, `I · 𝒪_X` is the ideal generated by the restrictions of the global
functions in `baseIdeal A I f`. -/
@[simp]
lemma baseIdealSheaf_ideal (U : X.affineOpens) :
    (baseIdealSheaf A I f).ideal U =
      Ideal.map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top (a := U.1))).op).hom (baseIdeal A I f) :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal _ _

/-- A global function in the image of `I` lies in `baseIdeal A I f`. -/
lemma mem_baseIdeal {a : A} (ha : a ∈ I) :
    ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv ≫ f.appTop).hom a ∈ baseIdeal A I f :=
  Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha

/-- `baseIdeal` is monotone in the ideal of the base. -/
lemma baseIdeal_mono (h : I ≤ J) : baseIdeal A I f ≤ baseIdeal A J f :=
  Ideal.map_mono h

/-- `I · 𝒪_X` is monotone in the ideal of the base. -/
lemma baseIdealSheaf_mono (h : I ≤ J) : baseIdealSheaf A I f ≤ baseIdealSheaf A J f :=
  fun _ ↦ Ideal.map_mono (baseIdeal_mono A I J f h)

/-- The unit ideal of the base induces the unit ideal of global functions. -/
@[simp]
lemma baseIdeal_top : baseIdeal A ⊤ f = ⊤ :=
  Ideal.map_top _

/-- The unit ideal of the base induces the unit ideal sheaf `⊤` on `X`. -/
@[simp]
lemma baseIdealSheaf_top : baseIdealSheaf A ⊤ f = ⊤ :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext <| funext fun U ↦ by
    rw [baseIdealSheaf_ideal, baseIdeal_top, Ideal.map_top, Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_top,
      Pi.top_apply]

/-- The zero ideal of the base induces the zero ideal of global functions. -/
@[simp]
lemma baseIdeal_bot : baseIdeal A ⊥ f = ⊥ :=
  Ideal.map_bot

/-- The zero ideal of the base induces the zero ideal sheaf `⊥` on `X`. -/
@[simp]
lemma baseIdealSheaf_bot : baseIdealSheaf A ⊥ f = ⊥ :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext <| funext fun U ↦ by
    rw [baseIdealSheaf_ideal, baseIdeal_bot, Ideal.map_bot, Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_bot,
      Pi.bot_apply]

/-- Forming the induced ideal of global functions is multiplicative. -/
lemma baseIdeal_mul : baseIdeal A (I * J) f = baseIdeal A I f * baseIdeal A J f :=
  Ideal.map_mul _ _ _

/-- Forming `I · 𝒪_X` is multiplicative. -/
lemma baseIdealSheaf_mul :
    baseIdealSheaf A (I * J) f = baseIdealSheaf A I f * baseIdealSheaf A J f :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext <| funext fun U ↦ by
    rw [baseIdealSheaf_ideal, baseIdeal_mul, Ideal.map_mul, Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_mul,
      Pi.mul_apply, baseIdealSheaf_ideal, baseIdealSheaf_ideal]

/-- The ideal of global functions induced by `I ^ n` is the `n`-th power of the one induced
by `I`. -/
lemma baseIdeal_pow (n : ℕ) : baseIdeal A (I ^ n) f = baseIdeal A I f ^ n :=
  Ideal.map_pow _ _ _

/-- The ideal sheaf `I ^ n · 𝒪_X` is the `n`-th power of `I · 𝒪_X`. This is what identifies
the two readings of the subsheaf `I ^ n 𝒪_X` of [Stacks, Section 02O7]. -/
lemma baseIdealSheaf_pow (n : ℕ) :
    baseIdealSheaf A (I ^ n) f = baseIdealSheaf A I f ^ n :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext <| funext fun U ↦ by
    rw [baseIdealSheaf_ideal, baseIdeal_pow, Ideal.map_pow, Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_pow,
      Pi.pow_apply, baseIdealSheaf_ideal]

end Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions

end
